description:
globs:
alwaysApply: true
---
- Preserve detailed comments, especially JSDocs documenting code functionality or intent. DO NOT remove them.
- When adding comments, prioritize explaining the 'why' (the reasoning or intent behind the code) rather than the 'what' (a simple description of the code's function).
- Only add comments explaining 'what' the code does if the implementation is particularly complex, cryptic, or follows an unconventional pattern.
- When necessary, these comments can be large and thorough
- DO NOT add comments that merely describe recent changes or edits made to the code.
- Never remove `TODO:` comments that are potentially still important technical debts

// Bad: Explains history/commented code
// Removed old sorting logic // const oldSort = ...
// type OldType = ... // Replaced by NewType

// Good: Explains 'why' or complex 'what'
// Fetch user data on mount to ensure profile is available
// This complex regex handles international phone numbers (see issue #123)
// Ensure shrinking only when wrapping or when only one badge is visible in auto mode to use most of the available real estate
